      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If it's something personal, Discord is fine, and if it's something long, you can meet in person in VRC. If you're using chat with players in other instances and looking at the overlay so many times that it becomes a hassle, it doesn't have to be VRC.I think VRC should devote resources to being VRC.\n\nIt's easy to say it's convenient, but maintaining it is too much of a hassle considering it's not at the core of the VRC experience. If you want to have a conversation with a user on another instance that goes beyond responding to \"Can I come and see you now?\", it no longer needs to be VRC.",
